# Documents in docs/

`docs/` holds team agreements: commits, branches, pull requests, and naming. Site copy lives in `i18n/messages/`, not here.

## Write

- One topic per file. Name the file in kebab-case, for example `pull-request-workflow-guidelines.md`.
- Write in English, in the same tone as the existing guides.
- Open with a title and one short paragraph on why the agreement exists.
- State the rule, then show a concrete example of the expected form.
- Keep the steps clear enough for a new teammate who has not read the code.

## Leave out

- Secrets, tokens, and personal data. This repository is public.
- A second copy of a rule that already has its own file. Link that file instead.
- How a Foundation page behaves. That belongs in product texts, not in these agreements.

## Example

```markdown
# Commit message

Use Conventional Commits so review history stays readable.

## Format

feat(archive): add fund search
```
